From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] libcutils: no error line when the kernel has no ftrace

The first trace of every process opens /sys/kernel/debug/tracing/trace_marker.
A kernel built without ftrace does not have it, so each process started logged
"Error opening trace file: No such file or directory (2)": 85 lines in one
session on this device (PW3 Android, Test V48), none of them about anything
that went wrong. Tracing is disabled either way.

ENOENT is now silent, and any other error still logged: a file that exists but
cannot be opened is a configuration mistake, while its absence is how the
kernel was built.

--- a/libcutils/trace-dev.c
+++ b/libcutils/trace-dev.c
@@ -163,7 +163,12 @@
 {
     atrace_marker_fd = open("/sys/kernel/debug/tracing/trace_marker", O_WRONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
     if (atrace_marker_fd == -1) {
-        ALOGE("Error opening trace file: %s (%d)", strerror(errno), errno);
+        /* A kernel built without ftrace has no trace_marker, and every process
+         * logged an error the first time it traced. Keep the error for a kernel
+         * that has the file but does not give it: that is a configuration
+         * mistake, while its absence is what the kernel was built as. */
+        if (errno != ENOENT)
+            ALOGE("Error opening trace file: %s (%d)", strerror(errno), errno);
         atrace_enabled_tags = 0;
         goto done;
     }
